# Current Engineering Protocol

- Read `AGENTS.md` before work. Explicit founder decisions, current source, real data obligations and verified tests override historical briefs.
- Inspect the full dependency chain needed to make a safe decision. For audits, repository-wide discovery is appropriate; never mistake a small file slice for proof of safety.
- Use Next.js and React versions from `package.json` (currently Next.js 16 and React 19). Do not force optional framework features or API patterns without requirement.
- Prefer maintainable, accessible, testable changes; token count and novelty are not architectural goals.
- Preserve approved homepage visual/interaction behavior unless change is specifically approved.
- Plan reversible changes on a feature branch and document scope, assumptions and rollback.
- Verify rendered behavior, mobile interaction, security boundaries, static/dynamic assets and data contracts in addition to types, lint and build.
- Never merge, deploy, change production configuration, or delete customer records without founder approval.
